The next shop has beautiful things.
I see a small stall.
There are many colourful items there.
I spot a beautiful ceramic mug.
It has a nice design on it.
I take that mug in my hand.
I ask the shopkeeper, "Dada, what is the price of this mug?"
The shopkeeper says, "Madam, it is for four hundred rupees."
Four hundred rupees!
Oh my, this mug is very expensive.
My budget is low.
I gently put the mug down.
I look at the shopkeeper and smile.
I say politely, "Dada, this mug is very beautiful."
"But I do not want it right now."
"Thank you."
The shopkeeper nods.
I walk towards the next stall.
